"""DGP7 second freeze + manifests (derived from dgp6_manifests.py; PROTOCOL.md sections 2-6). `freeze` writes FREEZE.json (implementation, configuration, runner / analyzer / oracle / probe / validator identities, native build + dependency identities, the residual
profile and policy constants incl. the frozen time blocks, the oracle plan with the replay priority, the fresh recipes with the JSON seed rule (EVAL7 / ORACLE7 with the ORACLE7 `variant` key), the guard-subset definition, the confirmation rule, the verdict gates, the budget
incl. recorded reassignments; the EVAL7 / ORACLE7 fresh inputs NOT yet generated). `holdout` (run at the frozen commit from the clean detached checkout) VERIFIES byte-identical the 68 DGP6 main inputs, the 32 DGP6 oracle inputs (of which the 8 exposed strong n8 card-4
coupling-2 models form this round's exposed oracle panel) and the 18 / 13 preservation inputs, GENERATES the 8 fresh EVAL7 and 4 fresh ORACLE7 models (canonical JSON seed string + integer recorded per input), hash-binds everything and writes MODEL_MANIFEST.json + the
per-panel manifests consumed by run_dgp7.py / the oracle driver: MAIN (76 = 68 + 8 EVAL7), GUARD (the 24 historical DGP6 completions + the 8 pinned old hard failures), GATE (the four exposed strong card-4 anchors), ORACLE (12), PRESERVATION_18 / PRESERVATION_13,
POLICY8 (the eight-model diagnostic panel), FRESH (8). usage: dgp7_manifests.py freeze|holdout [--code-root ROOT]"""

